here we ended up. This was a politically driven event and we decided to treat it that way. One of the many things that NPR has said, now they've set up this disinformation panel with your tax money. NPR, by the way, they exist in Washington, DC, and a half a billion dollar building. They have their own sushi bar in this building. Believe it or not, unlike a lot of radio stations around the country where, you know, they have seven or eight radio stations in a given city in a different studio row and half of them have bodies in them. Half of them are completely automated and the rest live on a substantially reduced salary. But in PR, they're living high on the hawk. They literally have shows on NPR that it's a one hour show that runs on the weekend. They have a dozen people on staff. That's how high on the hog they live. That's what NPR does. Because you see, they're not beholden to news. They're not beholden to sponsors, although they'd have underwriting. So they really do have sponsors. And they certainly aren't beholden to ratings because they don't need ratings in Washington. Like in DC, they do really well in the ratings because everybody there's a leftist. But they need to be defunded. Because disinformation. It's all nonsense. You've been fed a whole lot of nonsense. Nancy Pelosi's drunk drive and husband, Paul being blasted for buying $5 million shares in semiconductor firm days before the congressional vote that could hand $52 billion to chip manufacturers. But you know what, there's nothing to see here. This is clearly disinformation and misinformation. I know that the, you know, the, the Pelosi's are worth approximately $135 million. Actually, Paul Pelosi is worth $135 million, by the way. And Nancy Pelosi is ranked 14th wealthiest member of Congress. Her estimated net worth is $46 million. How is this possible? How is it possible that a someone who's representing the public who makes $170,000 a year is able to amass such a foreshit? It's like they almost had some insider information. It's just weird how that happens. Here's Nancy Pelosi talking about insider trading just a while",
